# This repository has no submodules.
#
# This file is intentionally present so that git and GitHub Desktop
# treat this repository as having zero active submodule definitions.
#
# If your local clone keeps showing a submodule fetch error when pulling
# (NeMo-Agent-Toolkit, vscode-pull-request-github, etc.) please follow
# the fix instructions in GIT_UPDATE_GUIDE.md — the quickest fix is a
# fresh clone:
#
#   1. File → Remove Repository in GitHub Desktop (does NOT delete files)
#   2. Delete the local folder
#   3. File → Clone Repository → POINTYTHRUNDRA654/desktop-tutorial
#
# Or from a terminal inside the repo folder:
#   git submodule deinit --all -f
#   git pull origin master
